{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "codeeval-v1",
  "description": "Reproducible code-retrieval corpus for Phase 18H. Public repositories only, pinned to exact commits, each size-capped so the whole suite runs inside a declared budget on a laptop. Replaces 'point it at whatever is in ~/Aniket', which was private, drifting, and unbounded — three attempts at it never finished.",
  "budget_seconds": 2400,
  "notes": [
    "`pin` is null until `mnesio-bench manifest pin` resolves it. SHAs are never hand-written: an invented commit is a benchmark nobody can reproduce, which is the exact failure this file exists to prevent.",
    "`max_files` is a hard guard, not a hint. A repository that exceeds it is SKIPPED and reported, never silently truncated — truncation would change the corpus without changing the manifest.",
    "`subdir` narrows indexing to one part of a large repository. It is part of the corpus definition and must be identical for every re-run.",
    "Sizes below are intentionally modest. The point is a suite a third party can re-run in under an hour, not the largest corpus we can name."
  ],
  "repos": [
    {
      "name": "ripgrep",
      "url": "https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep",
      "language": "rust",
      "subdir": "crates/core",
      "max_files": 60,
      "queries": 60,
      "pin": "3fce3b5bb0236da2df6d99672afb8a719642eca7"
    },
    {
